     <period-end iso-date="2019-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="0"></target>
     <actual value="14.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">19-05-2021: The project managed to benefit 14 members of staff through capacity building in 1. Water treatment 2. Waste Management - August 2020 and  3. Topography December 2020.  Participants gained hands-on experience in water treatment with reverse osmosis, learnt how to design own reverse osmosis unit, better operate own installations, and make better decisions about investment and maintenance as well.  The course provided a unique combination of scientific knowledge, virtual practice and appropriate techniques to design a water treatment system.  The course for Waste Management helped staff members identify ways to improve the Centre&apos;s existing practices, waste reduction, handling hazardous waste (following health and safety guidelines, keeping dangerous waste secure), collecting waste (storing it safely, sorting it for recycling) as well as implementing environmental management systems (improving overall processes in order to reduce waste and lessen the environmental impact).</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
